NEUTRAL TECHNIQUE FACTS (score-blind allowed packet):
- Technique: word-by-word spoken-state highlight sweep. On a black stage, one line-chunk at a time sits centered, fully pre-lit in the unspoken color; at each word's spoken onset a soft gradient sweep runs left-to-right through the word's letters from the unspoken color to the spoken color; the currently-sweeping word lifts above the baseline while it sweeps and settles after its visual fill completes; after the last word the completed chunk holds fully spoken-colored with baseline restored.
- Specimen: Packet #11 "Caption with Intention" sync demo, source 39.50-47.50 s segment; 17 words in 4 chunks (ASR onsets 40.18-46.12 s); label card "Synchronization" 39.56-40.20 s precedes the demo inside the segment.
- Census-anchor mapping (segment-relative ms; the build's prescribed state at each instant, from the filed Plan + amendment): 1100 Caption mid-sweep, front within the word, L1 others unfilled - 2800 front(animation,) in letters 3-7 of 9 - 4100 front(synchronized) in letters 3-7 of 12 - 4900 front(precisely) in letters 5-9 of 9 (visual lag priced) - 6600 word "is" lifted with fill < 0.5 (lift leads color) - 7100 fill(spoken.) in (0.1,0.6) and "is" still lifted - 7600 every fill = 1, every lift = 0.
- The visual schedule is CONFIG data: measured visual windows for 8 words (census + 24 fps micro-census), engine-derived windows (visualLagMs + sweepFraction, tile-capped) for the rest; per-word lift envelopes; exact endpoint rule (every letter reaches its exact endpoint color at p = 1).


=== PACKET SECTION (digest.md T06) ===

### T06 — Word-by-word spoken-state highlight sweep (38–48 s)
- **Mechanics:** on black, a full caption line sits centered in white; as the voice speaks, each word flips from white to yellow AT ITS SPOKEN ONSET, left to right, so the line's spoken prefix is yellow and its unspoken remainder stays white: "Caption with Intention uses" → "so captions are synchronized" → "precisely as each word is spoken." (at 44 s "each" has just flipped; by 46 s the line is fully yellow). The flip is a color-state change per word; the line does not move. The change is not instantaneous: the 40–47 s clip shows a mid-word state at ~42 s ("dynamic" fully yellow, "text" split yellow/white mid-word, "animation" still white) — the spoken state sweeps through the word as it is spoken, at letter scale. Synchronization here is DEMONSTRATED as speech-associated state flips on frames; the film's grid (T05) names the design — Roboto Flex variable axes — while automatic real-time operation remains UNVERIFIED (P-A1).
- **Why it works:** progress through the line is visible at every instant — the reader always knows where the voice is, which is the exact failure T02's #1 named.
- **Evidence:** ev/t044-sync-highlight-mid.jpg (mid-sweep: spoken prefix yellow, remainder white) · ev/t046-sync-highlight-complete.jpg (the completed line, fully yellow). Clip: clips/040-sync-highlight-7s.mp4 (40–47 s).


