## Swap test (§5 leg 1) — exact altered values + result
Altered sentence: L1 `Reading follows the voice` / L2 `exactly as it is spoken` with the exact onsets in amendment §6 · timing: derivation sweepFraction 0.55 → 1.0 · palette: spokenColor #f0ff05 → #ff9f1c. Result: **PASS** — all Class I assertions hold on the swap schedule (I1–I5 above), the endpoint color under the swap palette is rgb(255,159,28) vs the specimen's rgb(240,255,5), and exclusivity survives the retiming (I5). The technique reads from CONFIG alone; no code change.

## Purity (§5 leg 2) — raw grep output
Pattern (guards.md command 1 / plan §2.5) over recreation.html: `segment\.mp4|source\.mp4|<video|<img|\.jpg|\.mp4` → **grep exit 1, zero hits** (both pattern forms run; no url(#id) hits exist to classify). Asset inventory: recreation.html loads NOTHING external — no fonts, images, scripts, or media; every asset is code in the one file. comparison.html loads segment.mp4 (the labeled ORIGINAL side) + recreation.html (iframe) only.

## Comparison check (§5 leg 3)
comparison.html: video (segment.mp4, 8.000 s) beside the live recreation iframe; ONE control set (Play/Pause + Restart in the comparison only — the recreation's own bar is its standalone form); the recreation is slaved to the video's currentTime via its T195.seek hook on a shared rAF tick (shared start on Play/Restart); labels exactly `ORIGINAL — Caption with Intention @ 0:40–0:47` / `RECREATION — T195 spoken-state highlight sweep, parameterized`; durations matched (both 8000 ms); phone stacking via @media (max-width:700px) column layout with the control bar below, buttons ≥ 48 px. Verified at source level (PIXEL-UNVERIFIED limitation above).
Syntax: `node --check` on the recreation's extracted inline script — OK. Recreation script contains no RNG (deterministic pure state function; seeded-RNG census not applicable).

## A6 legs (pre-wave, on the final build)
- fit-table.md — HITs 0 in its cured form: post-fit rendered-geometry measurements (PIL/Liberation Sans instrument named in the table): ink widths 113.12–238.75 px vs the 331.2 px bound at the 360 px stage, full ink height 15.00 px and cap height 11.12 px, both ≥ the ~11 px floor. (First-filed form: formula-model rows — priced HITs by jev-prewave and replaced; see §Prewave.)
- config-census.md — HITs 0 (all keys resolved to value-flow sites; no CSS variables exist to strand; no subject-shaping literal outside CONFIG — two draft-stage exceptions cured into CONFIG before the census ran, recorded in the census).
Both outputs are fed verbatim into the jev-prewave payload (A10.1).

## Prewave (INSTRUCTION §5 leg 3b) — HOLD → cure → re-fire
First firing (payload codex/payload-prewave.txt, 54,290 B): **HOLD**, primary classification ASSERTED-CHECKS; dimensions parameterization 1.0 · purity pre-check 1.0 · own-checks completeness 0.25 · fidelity-plan honesty 1.0. Raw return filed verbatim at artifact-root `jev-prewave.md` (156,514 B; the transport duplicated the verdict section inside the raw file — priced as ONE return, the Cycle-035 wave-gate pattern). Three findings, all APPLIED:
1. A11 evidence — SF instants filed as "census instant" without their CONFIG expressions, and Class I instant-movement unsupported for I3/I4. Cure: expressions filed per row in the mapping above (`sourceAnchorMs − segmentStartS×1000` for SF; the named timing input for each Class I probe) + harness v2 mutation receipts (SF-MUT · MUT I1–I4) with before→after instants.
2. Measured fit — the fit table's rows were formula-model products, HITs under guard-measured-fit check 2. Cure: fit-table re-measured as post-fit rendered geometry (PIL/Liberation Sans, instrument + limit printed in the table); fontPx raised 82 → 86 (inside the amendment D9 measured bounds [76,88]) so the cap-height reading of the floor also clears (11.12 px ≥ ~11).
3. Harness receipt — v1's printed block carried 19 PASS lines against SUMMARY 20 (the excluded tautological line). Cure: harness v2 (tautology removed; the complete raw output is filed above; 28 PASS lines = SUMMARY pass=28).
Disposition: cures executed, own checks re-run on the final build (SUMMARY 28/0), A6 legs re-filed, prewave re-fired once on the cured record.

## Deviations / departures recorded
- D6–D10: amendment §9 (defaults re-priced from the micro-census).
- D11 (found in Execute, recorded here): the measured windows of `is` [46560,46710] and `spoken.` [46560,46750] OVERLAP — the film fills the final two words in one continuous front pass (micro-census finding 3). The amendment §5's "measured windows stand with gaps" wording therefore holds for 15 of 17 words; the tail pair is the priced exception, and transition exclusivity is asserted where the amendment asserts it — on derived/retimed schedules (I5) — while the specimen's tail overlap is the measured source state, not a construction defect.
- Packet prose departures D1–D5 stand from the Plan (lift exists · completion at 47.1 · four chunks · fraction+softness as CONFIG slack · trailing tint no-claim) — D4/D5 are now settled by the micro-census as filed above.


=== recreation.html (FULL SOURCE, the build under score) ===

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>T195 — spoken-state highlight sweep, parameterized</title>
<style>
  html,body{margin:0;padding:0;background:#111;min-height:100%;}
  body{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;}
  #stage{position:relative;width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/9;overflow:hidden;}
  #chunk{position:absolute;left:0;right:0;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;}
  .word{display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;}
  .sp{display:inline-block;}
  #labelCard{position:absolute;left:0;right:0;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;}
  #bar{display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:10px;background:#1c1c1c;width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;}
  #bar button{min-height:44px;min-width:64px;font-size:15px;border:1px solid #555;border-radius:8px;background:#2a2a2a;color:#eee;cursor:pointer;}
  #clock{color:#bbb;font-size:14px;min-width:120px;text-align:center;}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="stage">
  <div id="labelCard"></div>
  <div id="chunk"></div>
</div>
<div id="bar">
  <button id="btnPlay" type="button">Pause</button>
  <button id="btnRestart" type="button">Restart</button>
  <span id="clock">0 ms</span>
</div>
<script>
"use strict";
/* T195 — spoken-state highlight sweep (Packet #11 P11-T06), parameterized recreation.
   Construction: DOM per-letter spans inside per-word wrappers inside one mounted chunk;
   a single rAF clock; state is a pure function of segment-relative time.
   Visual schedule is CONFIG data (amendment-cycle035 §3): measured visual windows where
   the census/micro-census measured them, engine-derived windows elsewhere. */
const CONFIG = {
  segmentStartS: 39.5,
  totalMs: 8000,
  bgColor: "#000000",
  unspokenColor: "#dedede",
  spokenColor: "#f0ff05",
  fontStack: "\"Roboto Flex\", Roboto, Arial, sans-serif",
  fontPx: 86,
  fitWidthFraction: 0.92,
  sweepFraction: 0.55,
  visualLagMs: 120,
  minSweepMs: 120,
  frontSoftnessLetters: 3.5,
  liftPx: 28,
  liftRiseMs: 120,
  liftSettleMs: 120,
  chunkLeadMs: 60,
  stageRefWidthPx: 1920,
  wordSpaceEm: 0.28,
  lineTopFraction: 0.46,
  stageAspect: "16:9",
  labelCard: { show: true, text: "Synchronization", startSourceMs: 39560, dissolveStartSourceMs: 39980, endSourceMs: 40200 },
  lines: [
    { words: [
      { text: "Caption", onsetSourceMs: 40180, endSourceMs: 40820, visualOnsetSourceMs: 40280, visualEndSourceMs: 40750 },
      { text: "with", onsetSourceMs: 40820, endSourceMs: 40960 },
      { text: "Intention", onsetSourceMs: 40960, endSourceMs: 41200 },
      { text: "uses", onsetSourceMs: 41200, endSourceMs: 41560 }
    ]},
    { words: [
      { text: "dynamic", onsetSourceMs: 41560, endSourceMs: 41920, visualOnsetSourceMs: 41675, visualEndSourceMs: 41860 },
      { text: "text", onsetSourceMs: 41920, endSourceMs: 42180, visualOnsetSourceMs: 41930, visualEndSourceMs: 42090 },
      { text: "animation,", onsetSourceMs: 42180, endSourceMs: 42480, visualOnsetSourceMs: 42190, visualEndSourceMs: 42400 }
    ]},
    { words: [
      { text: "so", onsetSourceMs: 42960, endSourceMs: 43040 },
      { text: "captions", onsetSourceMs: 43040, endSourceMs: 43300 },
      { text: "are", onsetSourceMs: 43300, endSourceMs: 43500 },
      { text: "synchronized", onsetSourceMs: 43500, endSourceMs: 44040, visualOnsetSourceMs: 43510, visualEndSourceMs: 43700 }
    ]},
    { words: [
      { text: "precisely", onsetSourceMs: 44040, endSourceMs: 44420, visualOnsetSourceMs: 44170, visualEndSourceMs: 44470 },
      { text: "as", onsetSourceMs: 44420, endSourceMs: 44880 },
      { text: "each", onsetSourceMs: 44880, endSourceMs: 45200 },
      { text: "word", onsetSourceMs: 45200, endSourceMs: 45560 },
      { text: "is", onsetSourceMs: 45560, endSourceMs: 46120, visualOnsetSourceMs: 46560, visualEndSourceMs: 46710 },
      { text: "spoken.", onsetSourceMs: 46120, endSourceMs: 47140, visualOnsetSourceMs: 46560, visualEndSourceMs: 46750 }
    ]}
  ]
};

/* Optional URL override: ?config=<urlencoded JSON> deep-merges over CONFIG (swap-test route). */
function applyUrlConfig(cfg) {
  try {
    const raw = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get("config");
    if (!raw) return cfg;
    const over = JSON.parse(raw);
    const merge = (a, b) => {
      if (Array.isArray(b)) return b;
      if (b && typeof b === "object") { const o = Object.assign({}, a); for (const k in b) o[k] = merge(a ? a[k] : undefined, b[k]); return o; }
      return b;
    };
    return merge(cfg, over);
  } catch (e) { return cfg; }
}

function clamp01(x) { return x < 0 ? 0 : (x > 1 ? 1 : x); }
function hexRgb(h) { return [parseInt(h.slice(1, 3), 16), parseInt(h.slice(3, 5), 16), parseInt(h.slice(5, 7), 16)]; }
function lerpColor(a, b, f) {
  const ca = hexRgb(a), cb = hexRgb(b);
  return "rgb(" + Math.round(ca[0] + (cb[0] - ca[0]) * f) + "," + Math.round(ca[1] + (cb[1] - ca[1]) * f) + "," + Math.round(ca[2] + (cb[2] - ca[2]) * f) + ")";
}

/* Derive the visual schedule: measured overrides stand; other windows derive from
   onset + visualLagMs over (end-onset) x sweepFraction, tile-capped at the next
   word's visual onset inside the chunk (amendment §3/§5). All times returned
   segment-relative ms. */
function deriveSchedule(cfg) {
  const base = cfg.segmentStartS * 1000;
  return cfg.lines.map((line) => {
    const ws = line.words.map((w) => {
      const onset = w.onsetSourceMs - base, end = w.endSourceMs - base;
      let vOn, vEnd;
      if (typeof w.visualOnsetSourceMs === "number" && typeof w.visualEndSourceMs === "number") {
        vOn = w.visualOnsetSourceMs - base; vEnd = w.visualEndSourceMs - base;
      } else {
        vOn = onset + cfg.visualLagMs;
        vEnd = vOn + Math.max(cfg.minSweepMs, (w.endSourceMs - w.onsetSourceMs) * cfg.sweepFraction);
      }
      return { text: w.text, onset: onset, end: end, vOn: vOn, vEnd: vEnd, measured: typeof w.visualOnsetSourceMs === "number" };
    });
    for (let i = 0; i + 1 < ws.length; i++) {
      if (!ws[i].measured && ws[i].vEnd > ws[i + 1].vOn) ws[i].vEnd = ws[i + 1].vOn;
    }
    return { words: ws, mount: ws[0].onset - cfg.chunkLeadMs };
  });
}

function wordState(cfg, w, t) {
  const n = w.text.length;
  const p = clamp01((t - w.vOn) / (w.vEnd - w.vOn));
  const front = p * (n - 1 + cfg.frontSoftnessLetters);
  const letterFills = [];
  let sum = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    const f = clamp01((front - i) / cfg.frontSoftnessLetters);
    letterFills.push(f); sum += f;
  }
  const meanFill = n ? sum / n : 1;
  let lift;
  if (t <= w.vEnd) {
    lift = cfg.liftPx * clamp01((t - w.onset) / cfg.liftRiseMs);
  } else {
    const s = clamp01((t - w.vEnd) / cfg.liftSettleMs);
    const easeOut = 1 - Math.pow(1 - s, 3);
    lift = cfg.liftPx * (1 - easeOut);
  }
  if (t < w.onset) lift = 0;
  return { text: w.text, p: p, front: front, letterFills: letterFills, meanFill: meanFill, lift: lift, vOn: w.vOn, vEnd: w.vEnd, onset: w.onset };
}

function stateAt(cfg, t) {
  const sched = deriveSchedule(cfg);
  let mounted = -1;
  for (let i = 0; i < sched.length; i++) {
    const nextMount = (i + 1 < sched.length) ? sched[i + 1].mount : cfg.totalMs;
    if (t >= sched[i].mount && t < nextMount) mounted = i;
  }
  const base = cfg.segmentStartS * 1000;
  const lc = cfg.labelCard;
  let label = { visible: false, opacity: 0 };
  if (lc && lc.show) {
    const ls = lc.startSourceMs - base, ld = lc.dissolveStartSourceMs - base, le = lc.endSourceMs - base;
    if (t >= ls && t < le) label = { visible: true, opacity: t < ld ? 1 : 1 - (t - ld) / (le - ld) };
  }
  return {
    t: t, mountedChunk: mounted, label: label,
    chunks: sched.map((line) => ({ mount: line.mount, words: line.words.map((w) => wordState(cfg, w, t)) }))
  };
}

if (typeof module !== "undefined" && module.exports) {
  module.exports = { CONFIG: CONFIG, deriveSchedule: deriveSchedule, stateAt: stateAt, wordState: wordState, lerpColor: lerpColor };
}

if (typeof document !== "undefined") {
  const CFG = applyUrlConfig(CONFIG);
  const stage = document.getElementById("stage");
  const chunkEl = document.getElementById("chunk");
  const labelEl = document.getElementById("labelCard");
  const clockEl = document.getElementById("clock");
  const btnPlay = document.getElementById("btnPlay");
  const btnRestart = document.getElementById("btnRestart");
  stage.style.background = CFG.bgColor;
  stage.style.aspectRatio = CFG.stageAspect.replace(":", "/");
  labelEl.textContent = CFG.labelCard ? CFG.labelCard.text : "";
  labelEl.style.fontFamily = CFG.fontStack;
  labelEl.style.color = CFG.spokenColor;
  chunkEl.style.fontFamily = CFG.fontStack;

  const measureCtx = document.createElement("canvas").getContext("2d");
  function fittedFontPx(chunkText) {
    const stageW = stage.clientWidth || CFG.stageRefWidthPx;
    let fp = CFG.fontPx * stageW / CFG.stageRefWidthPx;
    measureCtx.font = fp + "px " + CFG.fontStack;
    const w = measureCtx.measureText(chunkText).width;
    const bound = CFG.fitWidthFraction * stageW;
    if (w > bound) fp = fp * bound / w;
    return fp;
  }

  let wordSpans = [], letterSpans = [], curChunk = -2, curFont = 0;
  function buildChunk(idx, fp) {
    chunkEl.innerHTML = ""; wordSpans = []; letterSpans = [];
    if (idx < 0) { curChunk = idx; return; }
    CFG.lines[idx].words.forEach((w, wi) => {
      const wEl = document.createElement("span");
      wEl.className = "word";
      const letters = [];
      for (const ch of w.text) {
        const lEl = document.createElement("span");
        lEl.textContent = ch;
        wEl.appendChild(lEl); letters.push(lEl);
      }
      chunkEl.appendChild(wEl); wordSpans.push(wEl); letterSpans.push(letters);
      if (wi + 1 < CFG.lines[idx].words.length) {
        const sp = document.createElement("span"); sp.className = "sp"; sp.style.width = CFG.wordSpaceEm + "em"; chunkEl.appendChild(sp);
      }
    });
    chunkEl.style.fontSize = fp + "px";
    curChunk = idx; curFont = fp;
  }

  function render(t) {
    const st = stateAt(CFG, t);
    const stageW = stage.clientWidth || CFG.stageRefWidthPx;
    const scale = stageW / CFG.stageRefWidthPx;
    labelEl.style.top = (CFG.lineTopFraction * 100) + "%";
    labelEl.style.fontSize = (CFG.fontPx * scale) + "px";
    labelEl.style.opacity = st.label.visible ? String(st.label.opacity) : "0";
    if (st.mountedChunk >= 0) {
      const text = CFG.lines[st.mountedChunk].words.map((w) => w.text).join(" ");
      const fp = fittedFontPx(text);
      if (st.mountedChunk !== curChunk || Math.abs(fp - curFont) > 0.5) buildChunk(st.mountedChunk, fp);
      chunkEl.style.top = (CFG.lineTopFraction * 100) + "%";
      const words = st.chunks[st.mountedChunk].words;
      words.forEach((ws, wi) => {
        wordSpans[wi].style.transform = "translateY(" + (-ws.lift * scale) + "px)";
        ws.letterFills.forEach((f, li) => {
          letterSpans[wi][li].style.color = lerpColor(CFG.unspokenColor, CFG.spokenColor, f);
        });
      });
      chunkEl.style.visibility = "visible";
    } else {
      chunkEl.style.visibility = "hidden";
    }
    clockEl.textContent = Math.round(t) + " ms";
  }

  let playing = true, startStamp = null, pausedAt = 0, seekMs = null;
  function frame(ts) {
    if (seekMs !== null) { render(seekMs); requestAnimationFrame(frame); return; }
    if (playing) {
      if (startStamp === null) startStamp = ts - pausedAt;
      let t = (ts - startStamp) % CFG.totalMs;
      if (t < 0) t += CFG.totalMs;
      pausedAt = t;
      render(t);
    }
    requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  }
  requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  btnPlay.addEventListener("click", () => {
    playing = !playing;
    if (!playing) { startStamp = null; }
    btnPlay.textContent = playing ? "Pause" : "Play";
  });
  btnRestart.addEventListener("click", () => { pausedAt = 0; startStamp = null; seekMs = null; });
  window.T195 = {
    seek: (ms) => { seekMs = ms; render(ms); },
    release: () => { seekMs = null; },
    stateAt: (ms) => stateAt(CFG, ms),
    CONFIG: CFG
  };
}
</script>
</body>
</html>



